WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
Shine light into one end of
a long, thin strand of glass.

2
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.320
Curve the strand around a gentle bend.

3
00:00:07.370 --> 00:00:11.090
The light follows the curve,
and comes out at the far end.

4
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:13.990
Yet light can pass from glass into air.

5
00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:16.000
It just bends as it leaves.

6
00:00:16.050 --> 00:00:18.740
So why doesn't it leak
out through the side?

7
00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:21.590
How can light stay
trapped inside the strand,

8
00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.440
even when it bends?

9
00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.950
In this mission, you'll aim
a ray from glass towards air,

10
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.540
and tilt it, step by step.

11
00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.920
Then you'll calculate the critical
angle for glass and for water.

12
00:00:33.970 --> 00:00:38.930
Your mission: explain how light stays
trapped inside a thin glass strand,

13
00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:40.280
even when it bends.
